{"id": "EUVD-2026-97664", "enisaUuid": "fa03657c-3d4c-3abd-92b1-c09a1d08e5ea", "description": "Heym v0.0.5 before v0.0.113 contains a broken access control vulnerability that allows former collaborators to keep executing JWT-auth workflows by reusing scoped workflow:execute tokens after share removal. Attackers can mint a token with a TTL up to 10 years, which the owner cannot list or revoke, and repeatedly run the workflow consuming shared credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:54:11", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/heymrun/heym/security/advisories/GHSA-pwr6-6377-3cgv", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/heym-0.0.5-before-0.0.113-broken-access-control-via-workflow-execution-tokens"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7v8m-98rf-rgvw", "CVE-2026-109362"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e5bd2b19-883a-3822-bcf3-a835a4aee555", "product": {"name": "heym", "vendor": {"name": "heymrun"}}, "product_version": "0.0.5 <0.0.113"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e198ee18-28e1-3eed-a84e-3826c95467b4", "vendor": {"name": "heymrun"}}], "isExploited": false}